Z||000031||Zorba||12-19-2000||12:25 PM||||<B>Batboy...</B><P>As I understand it...that foam air cleaner is not very good for the v8 motor. Depending on heat, the foam can deteriorate and fall into the carburator. I Think edelbrock sells a triangular air clean that fits just as nice. I had one of those on my kitcar and everytime I accelerated it would suck the fiberglass decklid. It was like my decklid was breathing...moving up and down with each rev. I replaced that with a knn housing and filter. Much more power. .02c||||reg||7
Z||000032||Will||12-19-2000||02:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tina:<BR><B>Thanks for the pic<BR>Much appreciated, just one question<BR>How exacty does it mount to the block ?<P>See Jekyl and Hyde,and the X-mas Fiero<BR>here <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/Albumlist?u=1315468" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/Albumlist?u=1315468</A> <P>From the usually sweet,(unless somebody ....really.... tests my patience)<BR>ARCHIE,I AM STILL WAITING FOR MY TACH<P>Tina<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Tina, I looked at those pictures, and I just have to say... I'm in LOVE!<P>That aside... Did too much torque kill your trans? Do you have pictures or can you provide a description of what broke and how?<BR>Thanks.||||reg||1
